{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XEYPqfzK5tKBN8kdAxkegL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded externally).\n\n**Current state** (trusting source_code over prose):\n- **Complete**: `pkg/testutils` (difftest.go + tests), `pkg/sys` (fileinfo + platform files + tests), `pkg/format` (color, column, size + tests), `cmd/cat` (main.go + cat_test.go)\n- **Partially complete**: `cmd/sponge` (main.go exists, no test file in source_code, testfiles: 0 in code_status)\n- **Not started**: cmd/du, cmd/wc, cmd/ls, trivial utilities, tee, head, seq, ts\n\n**Current release focus**: Release 00.0 infrastructure is substantially complete. Release 01.1 (cat) is complete. Release 01.2 (sponge) has implementation but no differential tests — this is the earliest incomplete release.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 01.2 (sponge) is the earliest release with incomplete work. `cmd/sponge/main.go` exists implementing prd007-sponge R1-R5, but no `sponge_test.go` exists. Per P5 (dependency ordering) and P2 (split implementation and tests), the next task is the sponge differential test file.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/sponge differential tests (prd007 R1.1, R2.1, R3.1, R4.1)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd007-sponge.yaml (R1-R5 requirements for sponge utility)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.2.yaml (test cases for sponge use case)\n      - cmd/sponge/main.go (existing sponge implementation to verify)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference pattern for differential test file structure)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests API, NormalizeFunc type, ExpectedFiles map)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sponge covering stdin soaking, file write, append mode, and passthrough\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test prd007 R1.1: sponge reads all of stdin before writing to the output file. Verify by piping stdin content to sponge with a named output file and confirming the file contains the complete input via ExpectedFiles.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test prd007 R2.1: sponge writes soaked stdin to a named output file atomically via temp file and rename. Verify the output file exists with expected content and exit code is 0.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test prd007 R3.1: sponge -a appends stdin to an existing file rather than truncating it. Create a file with initial content, run sponge -a, and verify the output file contains original content followed by stdin content via ExpectedFiles.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test prd007 R4.1: when no file argument is given, sponge writes soaked stdin to stdout (passthrough mode). Verify stdout matches the stdin input and exit code is 0.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow cmd/cat/cat_test.go structure: TestMain builds the Go sponge binary into a temp directory via go build and locates the reference binary via exec.LookPath. Print skip message to stderr and exit 0 if the reference binary is not found on PATH.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"The reference binary is 'sponge' from Homebrew moreutils. Unlike coreutils (which use g- prefix like gcat, gls), moreutils binaries are installed without a prefix. Use exec.LookPath(\\\"sponge\\\") to locate it.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use testutils.DiffTest with the ExpectedFiles map to verify file content after sponge writes to a named output file. This is the established pattern for file-output utilities per prd001-testutils R5.1.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Each test function creates its own t.TempDir() for isolation. Use a local writeTestFile helper matching the pattern in cmd/cat/cat_test.go. Pass file paths as positional arguments in DiffTest.Args.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go compiles with no errors (go build ./cmd/sponge/...).\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"TestMain builds the Go sponge binary and locates the 'sponge' reference binary; skips all tests with exit 0 if the reference binary is not on PATH.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"At least one differential test covers passthrough mode (no file argument, stdin written to stdout).\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"At least one differential test covers write-to-file mode (named output file verified via ExpectedFiles).\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"At least one differential test covers append mode (-a flag with pre-existing file content verified via ExpectedFiles).\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"All tests use testutils.RunDiffTests with DiffTest structs for consistent differential comparison.\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/sponge/... passes with no warnings.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56424,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56424},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ecefcc5-a779-448e-aecf-be43c26ca2cc","uuid":"83a17ee8-a956